-pacific-companies-union-93-meridian/","line":58},{"title":"Watkins Carter - 2:1","target":"https://static-v2.boisedev.com/assets/f002ca13-0527-4831-9254-99ce5fa33461.jpg","line":62,"embedded":true},{"title":"Watkins Carter - 2:1","target":"https://static-v2.boisedev.com/assets/f002ca13-0527-4831-9254-99ce5fa33461.jpg","line":74,"embedded":true},{"title":"Watkins Carter - 2:1","target":"https://static-v2.boisedev.com/assets/f002ca13-0527-4831-9254-99ce5fa33461.jpg","line":84,"embedded":true}],"metadata":{"title":"Meridian, Ada Co. consider tax increases and clawing back forgone taxes to fund rising expenses","source":"https://boisedev.com/news/2026/06/22/meridian-ada-co-consider-tapping-forgone-taxes-to-fund-rising-expenses/?utm_source=boisedev-email&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=boisedev-am","author":["[[Erin Banks Rusby - BoiseDev Reporter]]"],"published":"2026-06-22","created":"2026-07-08","description":"As local governments in Idaho grapple with the effects of past legislation, increasing costs, and some decreasing revenues, leaders are contemplating how to keep governments functional. BoiseDev took a look at the factors shaping the City of Meridian and Ada County’s proposed budgets for fiscal year 2027, which begins on October 1, 2026.  During budget […]"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},